@section builtintable.h

There are over 170 functions having names that start with @code{__},
that return a @code{PValue} and have an argument list of @code{(PNode*,
Context*, bool*)} that are declared in this file.

They are, at the time of this writing, defined in the files
@code{builtinlist.c}, @code{builtin.c}, @code{builtintable.c},
@code{extra.c}, @code{intrpevent.c}, @code{intrpfamily.c},
@code{intrpgnode.c}, @code{intrpmath.c}, @code{intrpperson.c},
@code{intrpseq.c}, @code{intrpstring.c}, and @code{rassa.c}.

The functions starting with @code{__} implement the DeadEnds script
functions.  To get the name of the script function that it implements,
remove the @code{__} at the start of the name.  In a handful of cases,
a script function has an alias.  If you do not find the implementation
of a script function after adding @code{__} to the start of its name,
then check the mapping in @code{functable.c}.

That said, an application will typically @b{NOT} call any of these
functions directly, but instead call them indirectly through the
script interpreter.

@section context.h

@defun createContext (Program*, Database*, File*) @arrow{} Context*
Creates a @code{Context} structure.

Usually not called directly by applications as @code{runProgram} calls
it to create a @code{Context*} for executing the script.
@end defun

@defun deleteContext (Context*) @arrow{} void
Deletes a @code{Context} structure.

Like @code{createContext}, not usually called directly by applications
as @code{runProgram} calls it after the script finishes executing.
@end defun

@defun createProgram (void) @arrow{} Program*
Creates a @code{Program} structure.  @b{NOTE}: Not usually called
directly as it creates an empty @code{Program*} structure.  Instead,
use @code{parseProgram} to call @code{createProgram} and initialize
the fields based on the files that were parsed.
@end defun

@defun deleteProgram (Program*) @arrow{} void
Deletes a @code{Program} structure.

@b{NOTE}: Not deleted by @code{runProgram} and friends as that allows
the same script to be run against multiple databases without having to
reparse the script.  When the script will no longer be executed, the
application should call @code{deleteProgram}.
@end defun

@defun validateCalls (FunctionTable* procedures, FunctionTable* functions) @arrow{} void
Checks that the @code{procedures} and @code{functions} to be called by
a program are defined.

Called by @code{parseProgram} after the script has been parsed.

Applications do not normally need tro call it directly.
@end defun

@section interp.h

@defun initializeInterpreter (Database*) @arrow{} void
Currently sets @code{Perrors} to zero; does nothing else.

@b{Should} be modified to take two arguments -- a @code{Database*} and a
@code{Context*}, then it could set the database field of the context to the
supplied database.
@end defun

@defun parseProgram (CString fileName, CString searchPath, ErrorLog *errorLog) @arrow{} Program*
Searches for @code{fileName} along @code{searchPath}.  If found, it is
parsed.  If there are no errors, a @code{Program*} is returned.
Otherwise, @code{null} is returned.  Errors are returned in
@code{errorLog}.
@end defun

@defun runProgram (Program* program, Database* database, File* outfile) @arrow{} InterpType
Runs a DeadEnds script program.  The argument @code{program} is a
@code{Program*} as returned by @code{parseProgram}.  The
@code{database} is the @code{Database*} to run the script against.
And @code{outfile} specifies where to place the script output.
@end defun

@defun finishInterpreter (void) @arrow{} void
Should be called When the parse of the script program is no longer
needed, Currently does nothing.  @b{Should} be modified to take a
@code{Context*} argument and free the memory.
@end defun

@defun interpret (PNode*, Context*, PValue*) @arrow{} InterpType
The function @code{interpret} is called to interpret the previously
parsed program.
@end defun

@defun setScriptOutputFile (CString filename, bool append, CString *errorMessage) @arrow{} bool
@end defun

@deftypevar bool programParsing
A boolean, @code{true} when a script is being parsed, @code{false}
otherwise.
@end deftypevar

@deftypevar bool programRunning
A boolean, @code{true} when a script is running, @code{false}
otherwise.
@end deftypevar

@deftypevar bool programDebugging
When @code{true} some debugging information is printed.
@end deftypevar

