@section pvalue.h

@deftypevar int Perrors
Counts the errors encountered while parsing the program.  For the
errors themselves, consult the @code{errorLog} argument to
@code{parseProgram}
@end deftypevar

The remaining functions in this section are not typically called
directly by an application program.

@defun isGNodeType (PVType type) @arrow{} bool
Returns true if a PVType is one of the GNode types.
@end defun

@defun createStringPValue (CString) @arrow{} PValue
Creates a String PValue with the String in the heap.
@end defun

@defun isPValue (PValue value) @arrow{} bool
Checks a PValue for validity by checking its type.
@end defun

@defun isRecordType (PVType type) @arrow{} bool
Checks if a PValue is a Gedcom node type.
@end defun

@defun isGNodeType (PVType type) @arrow{} bool
Returns true if a PVType is one of the GNode types.
@end defun

@defun subPValues (PValue, PValue, bool* eflag) @arrow{} PValue
Subtract two PValues and returns their difference.
@end defun

@defun mulPValues (PValue, PValue, bool* eflag) @arrow{} PValue
Multiplies two PValues and returns their product.
@end defun

@defun divPValues (PValue, PValue, bool* eflag) @arrow{} PValue
Divides two PValues and returns their quotient.
@end defun

@defun modPValues (PValue, PValue, bool* eflag) @arrow{} PValue
Takes the modulus of two PValues.  Both values must be integers.
@end defun

@defun negPValue (PValue, bool* eflag) @arrow{} PValue
Negates a PValue which must be numeric.
@end defun

@defun expPValues (PValue, PValue, bool* eflag) @arrow{} PValue
Raises the first number to the power of the second.  They must be integers.
@end defun

@defun equalPValues (PValue, PValue) @arrow{} bool
Returns whether two PValue are equal.
@end defun

@defun coercePValue (PValue* pvalue, int newType, bool* errorFlag) @arrow{} void
@end defun

@defun clonePValue (const PValue* original) @arrow{} PValue*
Returns a heap-allocated copy of the given PValue.
If the value is a @code{PVString}, the underlying string is duplicated.
@end defun

@defun cloneAndReturnPValue (const PValue* original) @arrow{} PValue
Clones a copy of a PValue on the heap, but then makes a stack copy,
Frees the heap copy and returns the stack copy.
@end defun

@defun typeOfPValue (PValue) @arrow{} String
Returns the 'type' of a PValue as a String.
@end defun

@defun valueOfPValue (PValue) @arrow{} String
Returns the value of a `PValue` as a `String`.
The caller is responsible for freeing the `String`.
@end defun

@defun pvalueReferenceCount (PValue *pvalue) @arrow{} int
For those @code{PValue}s for which there is a reference count, it
returns it.  For other @code{PValue}s, it returns zero.
@end defun

@defun numericPValue (PValue value) @arrow{} bool
Checks if a PValue has numeric type.
@end defun

@defun* allocPValue (PVType type, VUnion value) @arrow{} PValue
Allocates a @code{PValue} in the heap.
@code{PValue}s are usually value types, but when stored in tables or
lists they must be in the heap.
@end defun

@defun freePValue (PValue* pvalue) @arrow{} void
Frees the memory of an allocated PValue.
@end defun

@defun addReferenceToPValue (PValue *pvalue) @arrow{} void
Increments the reference count for those @code{PValue}s which are countable.
@end defun

@defun releasePValue (PValue *pvalue) @arrow{} void
@end defun

